«
@@ ============================================================
@@ Element — a chemical element, as a tagged list
@@ Input : the atomic number Z, the symbol ("Fe") or the name ("Iron")
@@ Output: { Z: Symbol: Name: Ar°: Abridged: … Configuration: }, without the
@@         missing values; A, the mass number of the most stable isotope,
@@         only when there is no standard atomic weight.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  ⓁElmData
  { "Z" "Symbol" "Name" "Ar°" "Abridged" "A" "Group" "Period" "Family" "State"
    "Tmelt" "Tboil" "Density" "Electronegativity" "Ionization" "Configuration"
    "Isotope" "Fraction" "Most stable" "Isotope mass" }
  → r t
  «
    @ + would drop the tags: push the tagged values, then gather them
    0
    1 20 FOR i
      r i GET
      IF DUP "—" == THEN DROP ELSE t i GET →Tag SWAP 1 + END
    NEXT
    →LIST
  »
»
